  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "116",
  "quote": "A landlord shall not increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit without first giving the tenant at least 90 days written notice of the landlord’s intention to do so.",
  "reason": "The clause allows a rent increase with only 30 days' written notice, which contradicts section 116(1) of the Act requiring at least 90 days' written notice. Under section 4(1) of the Act, any provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with the Act is void."
}

